+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use LRU (Least Recently Used) cache eviction with a 300-second TTL on cache entries, replacing an earlier LFU (Least Frequently Used) policy; this recency-based eviction combined with time-based expiration was chosen for better performance on time-bounded cached data patterns and to ensure stale data is removed even when frequently accessed.
